{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "25", "m": "11", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "04", "S": "31"}}, "news": [{"title": "Ten spots in Gurugram to get temporary C&D waste storage facilities: Haryana CM", "para": "Gurgaon is embarking on a significant initiative by establishing ten temporary storage sites dedicated to managing construction and demolition waste effectively. Each planned site spans one hectare and will be fortified to prevent any debris spillage. Chief Minister Nayab Singh Saini underscored the urgency for a systematic approach to waste management during a recent meeting.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/ten-spots-in-gurugram-to-get-temporary-cd-waste-storage-facilities-haryana-cm/136151731?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-302396/136151731.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "SC disposes of building violation pleas; hoteliers in Mussoorie hope for relief", "para": "Recently, over 200 hotels and homestays in Mussoorie were served notices from the Mussoorie Dehradun Development Authority. Following the Supreme Court's decision on unlawful constructions and the misuse of residential zones, those affected can now seek assistance from local authorities. This brings a mixture of hope and concern for hoteliers as regulatory challenges persist, while municipal officials face criticism for inadequate enforcement of existing building rules.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/hospitality/sc-disposes-of-building-violation-pleas-hoteliers-in-mussoorie-hope-for-relief/136151686?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-229280/136151686.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "hospitality"}, {"title": "WSB Real Estate Partners exits six housing investments with 19-21% average IRR", "para": "WSB Real Estate Partners has exited six residential investments across major Indian markets including Bengaluru, the Mumbai Metropolitan Region, and the National Capital Region. With an impressive average internal rate of return ranging from 19% to 21%, these exits yielded returns at 1.4 times the initial investment. Notably, these transactions were completed ahead of the planned schedules set for April to November 2026.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/wsb-real-estate-partners-exits-six-housing-investments-with-19-21-average-irr/136148337?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-149706/136148337.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}